# Q3Doom - Quake Visuals (r_quakeVisuals 1): what Quake 3 asset replaces
# each Doom asset. Edit freely; vid_restart (or a map change) reloads it.
#
#   wall <TEXTURE> <shader> [scale]   a wall texture (TEXTURE1/2)
#   flat <FLAT> <shader> [scale]      a floor or ceiling flat
#   sky <SKYn> <shader>               the sky of an episode (SKY1 ... SKY4)
#   keep <NAME>                       keep the Doom texture or flat
#   item <doomednum> <model> [model2] [scale]   an item's 3D model
#
# Names may end with * (any suffix). The first matching line wins. A shader
# is a Quake 3 shader or image path; [scale] is world units per texel
# (default 0.5: a 256 pixel texture covers 128 units, as in Quake 3 maps).
# Anything not listed keeps its Doom look.

# --- kept Doom: gameplay signs and see-through middle textures --------------

keep SW1*
keep SW2*
keep EXIT*
keep DOORBLU*
keep DOORRED*
keep DOORYEL*
keep MIDGRATE
keep MIDBRN1
keep MIDVINE*
keep BRNSMAL*
keep BRNBIG*
keep AASTINKY
keep *POIS
keep GRAYDANG
keep PLANET1

# --- skies --------------------------------------------------------------------

sky SKY1 textures/skies/pjbasesky_arena1_sky
sky SKY2 textures/skies/killsky
sky SKY3 textures/skies/hellsky2
sky SKY4 textures/skies/tim_hell

